# Auto-push to GitHub

The user works on multiple machines and does not want to copy project folders by hand.

- Standing user authorization: commit and push each completed task without asking again.
- After committing, immediately push to the configured upstream. Use `git push`
  when local configuration supports it; if branch names differ, explicitly use
  `git push origin HEAD:<upstream-branch>`. For a new branch without an upstream,
  use `git push -u origin HEAD`.
- Verify that the remote branch points to the local commit before reporting sync complete.
- Remote: `origin` → `https://github.com/zillawillysu-a11y/CuePlayer_didido.git`
- Do not force-push to `main`/`master` unless the user explicitly asks.
- If push fails (auth/network), tell the user clearly and leave the commit local.
- Prefer committing + pushing meaningful slices when the user asks to save/sync work across machines.
